---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TrustBadge from '../components/TrustBadge.astro';
import SocialProof from '../components/SocialProof.astro';
import ScarcityBadge from '../components/ScarcityBadge.astro';
import UrgencyTimer from '../components/UrgencyTimer';

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    id: 'mangroomer-platinum',
    name: 'Mangroomer Ultimate Pro',
    category: 'Electric Back Shaver',
    price: 49.99,
    rating: 4.8,
    reviewCount: 12450,
    badge: 'Best Overall',
    bestFor: 'Most Men',
    imageUrl: 'https://placehold.co/600x400/1E90FF/white?text=Mangroomer+Ultimate+Pro',
    amazonUrl: 'https://amzn.to/4hFfjcg',
    pros: ['Extendable arm reaches essentially anywhere', 'Shock absorber flex neck preventing irritation', 'Two distinct heads: Trimmer & Foil', 'Power boost button for thick patches'],
    cons: ['Charging can take up to 8 hours', 'Plastic build feels slightly hollow'],
    specs: {
      'Reach': 'Extends to 135 degrees',
      'Power': 'Lithium Max Battery',
      'Blade Type': 'Hypoallergenic Foil + Trimmer',
      'Warranty': '2 Years'
    },
    bottomLine: "The 'Swiss Army Knife' of back shavers. If you want one tool to do it all without asking for help, this is it.",
    descriptionParagraphs: [
      "The Mangroomer Ultimate Pro isn't just a shaver — it's an engineering solution to a problem most men are too embarrassed to talk about. After more than a decade of R&D, Mangroomer has refined their flagship model into what we believe is the most versatile back shaver on the market today. Its signature feature is the 'Power Burst' button, which acts as a turbo mode for particularly dense patches of hair. During our 90-day testing period, this was the only electric shaver that never stalled or snagged, even on our tester with the thickest back hair.",
      "What really sets the Ultimate Pro apart is the dual-head system. You get two interchangeable attachment heads — a 1.8-inch trimmer for mowing down longer hair, and a hypoallergenic foil head for achieving that smooth, clean finish. The lock slider at the top makes swapping between them genuinely effortless — no tools, no fumbling. We found ourselves using the trimmer first to reduce hair length, then switching to the foil for the final pass. The result was consistently smoother than any single-head electric we tested.",
      "The shock absorber flex neck deserves special mention. Unlike rigid shavers that require you to contort your arm at bizarre angles and apply uneven pressure, the Mangroomer's multi-flex neck pivots to maintain constant contact with your skin. Combined with the patented 135-degree opening angle and an extendable handle that locks into place, it reaches areas you genuinely cannot see or feel with your hands. Our tallest tester (6'4\") confirmed he could reach his entire lower back without straining.",
      "The downsides? The 6-8 hour charge time is genuinely annoying — though the lithium battery does hold its charge for multiple sessions once topped up. The overall build quality feels more 'functional plastic' than 'premium grooming tool,' but after 90 days of regular use, nothing cracked, broke, or loosened. For $49.99, the Mangroomer Ultimate Pro delivers the best all-around back shaving experience we've tested. It's not perfect, but it's the closest thing to it."
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'bro-shaver-3',
    name: 'Bro Shaver 3.0',
    category: 'Manual Back Shaver',
    price: 13.99,
    rating: 4.5,
    reviewCount: 3200,
    badge: 'Best Budget Pick',
    bestFor: 'Budget Buyers',
    imageUrl: 'https://placehold.co/600x400/333333/white?text=Bro+Shaver+3.0',
    amazonUrl: 'https://amzn.to/4j3Y9Gy',
    pros: ['Uses standard DE safety razor blades (cheap refills)', 'Widest cutting head in class', 'Zero battery anxiety', 'Waterproof (because it\'s manual)'],
    cons: ['Higher learning curve (can nick if careless)', 'No flex neck'],
    specs: {
      'Reach': '20-inch Handle',
      'Refills': 'Standard DE Blades (Pennies)',
      'Blade Type': '3-Blade Tech',
      'Warranty': '60-Day Money Back'
    },
    bottomLine: "The most economical choice long-term. Almost free to run, but requires a steady hand.",
    descriptionParagraphs: [
      "The Bro Shaver 3.0 strips away every gimmick in the back shaving world and boils it down to a simple proposition: a really long handle with a really wide blade. It is, effectively, a giant rake for your back. But that's its genius. By utilizing standard Double Edge (DE) safety razor blades — the same ones your grandfather used — it solves the single biggest scam in men's grooming: overpriced proprietary cartridges. You need exactly 3 DE blades to fill the head, and a pack of 50 runs about five dollars. Do the math: that's roughly $0.30 per blade change. Try getting that from Gillette.",
      "The 3.0 model introduces something the original lacked: two shaving modes. A 'mild' setting for quick maintenance shaves when hair is short, and an 'aggressive' setting that exposes more blade for a closer cut on longer growth. The silicon handle with textured plastic strips provides a surprisingly secure grip, and at 20 inches, it's the longest handle in our test — ideal for taller men and bodybuilders who need extreme reach. The 3.7-inch blade span is also the widest we tested, which means fewer passes and faster sessions overall.",
      "Here's where honesty matters: the Bro Shaver has a real learning curve. Unlike the bakblade's safety teeth or the Mangroomer's guarded foil, the Bro Shaver uses exposed razor blades. If your blade alignment is off by even a millimeter, or you apply uneven pressure, you will nick yourself. Our testers experienced 3-4 small cuts during the first two sessions before they dialed in their technique. By week three, nicks dropped to zero. The key is light pressure and slow, deliberate strokes — treat it like a straight razor, not a disposable Bic.",
      "At $13.99 with a 60-day money-back guarantee, the Bro Shaver 3.0 is the ultimate budget pick for men who don't mind a brief learning period. Once you master the technique, you'll never pay for proprietary cartridges again. It's also fully waterproof by nature (no electronics), making it the only shaver on this list you can confidently use in a steamy shower without worrying about damage."
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'bakblade-2',
    name: 'bakblade 2.0 Elite',
    category: 'Manual Back Shaver',
    price: 29.95,
    rating: 4.7,
    reviewCount: 8500,
    badge: 'Smoothest Shave',
    bestFor: 'Closest Shave',
    imageUrl: 'https://placehold.co/600x400/FF4500/white?text=bakblade+2.0',
    amazonUrl: 'https://amzn.to/4j0CSNP',
    pros: ['DRYglide blades allow dry shaving without irritation', 'S-shaped ergonomic handle', 'Blades detach to use on chest/arms', 'Safety teeth technology'],
    cons: ['Proprietary blades are pricey', 'Bulky head can miss contours'],
    specs: {
      'Reach': '18-inch S-Shape',
      'Refills': 'Patented Cartridges',
      'Blade Type': 'DryGlide Technology',
      'Warranty': '30-Day Money Back'
    },
    bottomLine: "The closest you'll get to a barber's razor finish at home. The 'DryGlide' tech actually works.",
    descriptionParagraphs: [
      "If the Bro Shaver is a rake, the bakblade 2.0 Elite is a precision instrument. Its claim to fame is 'DryGlide' technology — a patented blade system designed to shave dry skin without cream, water, or any lubrication whatsoever. We were skeptical. Dry shaving sounds like a recipe for razor burn. But after three months of testing, we can confirm: it genuinely works. The secret is in the blade cartridge design. Each cartridge is shielded by rows of unique safety teeth that flatten the skin microseconds before the blade makes contact, mimicking the mechanics of a high-end barber's safety razor.",
      "The build quality on the bakblade 2.0 Elite is noticeably superior to everything else on this list. The handle incorporates several different types of plastic with varying textures and contours — ribbed sections for grip, smooth sections for sliding your hand into position, and a satisfying click when the S-shaped handle locks into its full 18-inch extension. The S-shape itself provides better leverage than straight handles because it naturally follows the curvature of your arm motion when reaching behind your back. It's a small detail, but it makes a meaningful difference during a 10-minute shaving session.",
      "Safety is where the bakblade truly dominates. Across our entire 90-day test — three volunteers, dozens of sessions each — not a single person drew blood. Not once. Compare that to the Bro Shaver (3-4 nicks in early sessions) and even the Mangroomer (one tester caught a mole). The very precise angle of the razor blade relative to the plastic teeth creates a geometry that's essentially cut-proof on flat skin. The blades also detach from the handle entirely, so you can use the cartridge head on your chest, arms, or shoulders without the long handle getting in the way.",
      "The catch? bakblade uses proprietary DryGlide cartridges that only they sell. You cannot substitute aftermarket blades or standard razors — the cartridge locks into a custom slot. A 4-pack of replacement cartridges runs about $15-20, which adds up over time. If ongoing cost is your primary concern, the Bro Shaver wins. But if you value the safest, smoothest shave with zero risk of cuts, the bakblade 2.0 Elite is worth every penny of its $29.95 entry price."
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'philips-norelco-5000',
    name: 'Philips Norelco Bodygroom 5000',
    category: 'Electric Body Groomer',
    price: 69.96,
    rating: 4.6,
    reviewCount: 35000,
    badge: 'Best For Sensitive Skin',
    bestFor: 'Sensitive Skin',
    imageUrl: 'https://placehold.co/600x400/228B22/white?text=Philips+Bodygroom+5000',
    amazonUrl: 'https://amzn.to/4iDcI3V',
    pros: ['Truly waterproof (shower safe)', 'Rounded tips prevent scratches', 'Dual-sided design', 'Lithium-ion battery (1 hour run time)'],
    cons: ['Back attachment is a bit shorter than others', 'Takes longer than wide-blade manuals'],
    specs: {
      'Reach': 'Modular Extension Arm',
      'Power': 'Lithium-ion',
      'Blade Type': 'Hypoallergenic Foil',
      'Warranty': '5 Years'
    },
    bottomLine: "The gentle giant. Ideally suited for men with sensitive skin or prone to 'backne'.",
    descriptionParagraphs: [
      "The Philips Norelco Bodygroom 5000 takes a fundamentally different approach to back hair. While the Mangroomer and manual shavers focus on raw cutting power and closeness, the Bodygroom 5000 prioritizes one thing above all else: skin safety. If you've ever shaved your back only to spend the next 48 hours dealing with angry red bumps, itching, or irritated moles, this is the shaver Philips designed specifically for you. It uses a hypoallergenic foil head with individually rounded blade tips that physically cannot dig into skin, even when pressed firmly against raised moles, acne, or uneven surfaces.",
      "During our testing, the Bodygroom 5000 was the only shaver that produced zero skin irritation across all three volunteers — including our tester who specifically struggles with 'backne' (back acne). The rounded tip technology prevents the micro-cuts that trigger inflammation, and the hypoallergenic foil means no allergic reactions for sensitive skin types. The dual-sided design gives you a trimmer on one end and a foil shaver on the other, so you don't need to swap heads like the Mangroomer. Just flip the tool over mid-session.",
      "The modular extension arm for back reach is functional but shorter than the competition. Our 6'4\" tester could reach most of his back but struggled with the very center of his lower back — the Mangroomer and Bro Shaver handled this spot more easily. However, the Bodygroom 5000 is fully waterproof (IPX7 rated), which means you can shave in the shower without worry. Hot water softens the bristles and opens pores, which further reduces irritation. The lithium-ion battery delivers a solid 60 minutes of runtime on a single charge — enough for 5-6 full back sessions.",
      "At $69.96, this is the most expensive option on our list, and it's not the closest shave. You'll feel light stubble about a day sooner than with the bakblade or Bro Shaver. But what you're paying for is comfort and skin health. If you've tried other back shavers and ended up with razor burn, bumps, or irritation every time, the Bodygroom 5000 solves that problem entirely. Plus, Philips backs it with an industry-leading 5-year warranty — a testament to how confident they are in the build quality."
    ]
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://thehonestreviewers.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Best Lists", "item": "https://thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Best Back Shavers", "item": "https://thehonestreviewers.com/best-mens-back-shavers/" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does shaving your back make the hair grow back thicker?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. This is a common myth. Shaving blunts the tip of the hair, which may make it feel coarser as it grows out, but it does not alter the follicle's growth rate or thickness." }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is electric or manual better for back shaving?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Manual shavers (like bakblade) offer a closer shave but have a higher risk of nicks. Electric shavers (like Mangroomer) are faster and safer for sensitive skin but may leave slight stubble." }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I shave my own back without help?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Every tool on this list is specifically designed for solo use with extended handles reaching 18-20 inches. The Mangroomer's 135-degree pivot and the bakblade's S-shape handle are engineered to reach areas you can't see." }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How often should I shave my back?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Most men maintain their back every 1-2 weeks. If you use an electric trimmer like the Mangroomer, you can touch up every 4-5 days. Hair growth rate varies, so find the rhythm that works for you." }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do back shavers cause ingrown hairs?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Back shavers are less likely to cause ingrown hairs than waxing because they cut at the surface. Shave with the grain, exfoliate weekly, and moisturize after to minimize risk. The bakblade's DryGlide tech is especially gentle." }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the cheapest way to remove back hair?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The Bro Shaver 3.0 at $13.99 is the most affordable option. It uses standard double-edge safety blades that cost about $0.10 each, making it the cheapest long-term solution by far." }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "4 Best Men's Back Shavers in 2026: Tested & Ranked",
      "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Alex Rivers" },
      "datePublished": "2026-01-15",
      "dateModified": "2026-02-18",
      "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "The Honest Reviewers" }
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      "name": product.name,
      "image": product.imageUrl,
      "description": product.descriptionParagraphs[0],
      "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": product.name.split(' ')[0] },
      "offers": {
        "@type": "Offer",
        "price": product.price,
        "priceCurrency": "USD",
        "availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
        "url": product.amazonUrl
      },
      "aggregateRating": {
        "@type": "AggregateRating",
        "ratingValue": product.rating,
        "reviewCount": product.reviewCount
      }
    }))
  ]
};
---

<Layout
  title="4 Best Men's Back Shavers (2026): Tested & Ranked | The Honest Reviewers"
  description="We tested 12+ back shavers over 90 days. Only 4 made the cut. See which back shaver wins for your body type, budget, and skin sensitivity."
  ogImage="https://placehold.co/1200x630/1E90FF/white?text=Best+Back+Shavers+2026"
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: '2026-01-15',
    modifiedTime: '2026-02-18',
    author: 'Alex Rivers',
    section: 'Grooming',
    tags: ['back shaver', 'mens grooming', 'back hair removal', 'body grooming', 'mangroomer', 'bakblade'],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "See #1 Pick on Amazon", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>

  <!-- ========== HERO SECTION ========== -->
  <div class="relative bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Subtle pattern overlay -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-5" style="background-image: url('data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg width=\'60\' height=\'60\' viewBox=\'0 0 60 60\' xmlns=\'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\'%3E%3Cg fill=\'none\' fill-rule=\'evenodd\'%3E%3Cg fill=\'%23ffffff\' fill-opacity=\'1\'%3E%3Cpath d=\'M36 34v-4h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2h-4zm0-30V0h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2V6h4V4h-4zM6 34v-4H4v4H0v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2H6zM6 4V0H4v4H0v2h4v4h2V6h4V4H6z\'/%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/svg%3E');"></div>

    <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
      <nav class="flex text-sm text-gray-400 mb-8">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-white no-underline text-gray-400">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-600">/</span>
        <a href="/best-of" class="hover:text-white no-underline text-gray-400">Best Lists</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-600">/</span>
        <span class="text-gray-300">Back Shavers</span>
      </nav>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center">
        <!-- Left: Copy -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-6">
            <TrustBadge />
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
              Updated Feb 2026
            </span>
          </div>

          <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-[1.08] tracking-tight mb-6">
            4 Best Men's Back Shavers:
            <span class="text-[#1E90FF]"> Say Goodbye to Back Hair</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed mb-8">
            We bought and tested 12+ back shavers over 90 days — measuring shave closeness, counting nicks, and timing regrowth. These are the <strong class="text-white">only 4 worth buying</strong> in 2026.
          </p>

          <!-- Author line -->
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
            <img src="https://i.pravatar.cc/80?img=33" alt="Alex Rivers" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full border-2 border-gray-700" />
            <div>
              <p class="text-white font-bold text-sm">Alex Rivers</p>
              <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">Grooming Editor &middot; 8+ Years Testing &middot; Updated Feb 18, 2026</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
            <a href="#mangroomer-platinum" class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg shadow-[#FF4500]/25 transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 no-underline text-center text-lg">
              See Our #1 Pick
            </a>
            <a href="#comparison-table" class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/15 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/20 transition-all no-underline text-center text-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
              Compare All 4
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: Winner Card -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl shadow-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 transform lg:rotate-1 hover:rotate-0 transition-transform">
            <div class="bg-[#FF4500] px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
              <div>
                <p class="text-white/70 text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest">Our #1 Pick</p>
                <p class="text-white font-black text-lg">{PRODUCTS[0].name}</p>
              </div>
              <span class="bg-white/20 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold">
                {PRODUCTS[0].badge}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-6">
              <img src={PRODUCTS[0].imageUrl} alt={PRODUCTS[0].name} class="w-full rounded-2xl mb-6" />
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
                <span class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900">${PRODUCTS[0].price}</span>
                <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
                  <div class="flex text-yellow-400">
                    {[...Array(5)].map((_, i) => (
                      <svg class={`w-4 h-4 ${i < Math.floor(PRODUCTS[0].rating) ? 'fill-current' : 'text-gray-200'}`} xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
                        <path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z" />
                      </svg>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                  <span class="text-gray-400 text-xs font-bold ml-1">{PRODUCTS[0].reviewCount.toLocaleString()}</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <ScarcityBadge count={7} />
              <a
                href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"
                class="mt-4 block w-full bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white text-center py-4 rounded-xl font-black text-lg shadow-lg transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 no-underline"
              >
                Check Price on Amazon &rarr;
              </a>
              <p class="text-center text-xs text-gray-400 mt-3">Free shipping with Prime</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== TRUST STRIP ========== -->
  <div class="bg-gray-50 border-y border-gray-100">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 text-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#1E90FF]">12+</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-500 font-medium mt-1">Back Shavers Tested</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#1E90FF]">90</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-500 font-medium mt-1">Days of Testing</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#1E90FF]">3</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-500 font-medium mt-1">Volunteer Testers</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-[#1E90FF]">$0</p>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-500 font-medium mt-1">Free Samples Accepted</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">

    <!-- ========== TABLE OF CONTENTS ========== -->
    <nav class="mb-16 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100 max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-4">In This Guide</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm font-medium list-none p-0 m-0">
        <li><a href="#comparison-table" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">Quick Comparison Table</a></li>
        <li><a href="#mangroomer-platinum" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">#1 Mangroomer Ultimate Pro (Best Overall)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#bro-shaver-3" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">#2 Bro Shaver 3.0 (Best Budget)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#bakblade-2" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">#3 bakblade 2.0 Elite (Smoothest Shave)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#philips-norelco-5000" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">#4 Philips Norelco Bodygroom 5000 (Best For Sensitive Skin)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#buying-guide" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">Back Shaver Buying Guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="#pro-tips" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">Pro Tips for a Perfect Back Shave</a></li>
        <li><a href="#faq" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline no-underline">FAQ</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <!-- ========== INTRO CONTENT ========== -->
    <section class="max-w-4xl mb-20">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">Why You Need a Dedicated Back Shaver</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-600 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          If you've ever twisted your arm awkwardly trying to reach that patch of hair between your shoulder blades, you know the struggle. Regular razors were not designed for your back. You risk cuts, miss entire patches, and end up frustrated.
        </p>
        <p>
          A purpose-built back shaver solves this with extended handles, wider blade heads, and ergonomic designs that match the contours of your back. The question is: electric or manual? Cheap or premium? That's what we set out to answer.
        </p>
      </div>

